# Contributing to {{project_name}}

## Prerequisites

{{prerequisites}}

You need [devenv](https://devenv.sh/getting-started/) for development, and [podman](https://podman.io) or Docker for CI checks. devenv provides everything else, including `make`, [pre-commit](https://pre-commit.com), [gitleaks](https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks) and [trivy](https://trivy.dev). [semgrep](https://semgrep.dev) runs in a container.

Run `make doctor` inside `devenv shell` to see what's missing.

## Setup

```bash
devenv shell
make setup
pre-commit install
```

Run the commands below inside `devenv shell`. Add new tools to `devenv.nix`, and commit `devenv.lock`.

## Everyday commands

| Command | Use it to |
| --- | --- |
| `make fmt` | Format code |
| `make lint` | Check formatting, run linters and type checks |
| `make build` | Make a debug build |
| `make test` | Run tests on the debug build |
| `make release` | Make a release build, which is what ships. It never signs or publishes |
| `make test-release` | Run tests on the release build |
| `make ci-check` | Run CI's checks in the CI container, as the server does |
| `make ci-release` | Build the release in the CI container. Only this kind of build ships, because one from devenv links to `/nix/store` |
| `make security` | Scan for secrets, insecure code, vulnerable dependencies and misconfigurations |
| `make docs` | Build API docs into `docs/api` |
| `make docs-check` | Check that functions and types have doc comments |
| `make check` | Run the checks in devenv: everything except the `ci-*` commands |

